        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "### Algorithm: Supervised GraphWise",
          "",
          "Supervised GraphWise is an inductive vertex representation learning algorithm which is able to leverage vertex feature information. It can be applied to a wide variety of tasks, including vertex classification and link prediction. ",
          "",
          "A Supervised GraphWise model consists of two graph convolutional layers followed by several prediction layers.  ",
          "The forward pass through a convolutional layer for a vertex proceeds as follows:  ",
          "* A set of neighbors of the vertex is sampled.",
          "* The previous layer representations of the neighbors are mean-aggregated, and the aggregated features are concatenated with the previous layer representation of the vertex.",
          "* This concatenated vector is multiplied with weights, and a bias vector is added.",
          "* The result is normalized to such that the layer output has unit norm.",
          "",
          "The prediction layers are standard neural network layers."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : {
          "startTime" : 1715010166264,
          "endTime" : 1715010166319,
          "interpreter" : "md",
          "taskStatus" : "SUCCESS",
          "status" : "SUCCESS",
          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<h3 id=\"algorithm-supervised-graphwise\">Algorithm: Supervised GraphWise</h3>\n<p>Supervised GraphWise is an inductive vertex representation learning algorithm which is able to leverage vertex feature information. It can be applied to a wide variety of tasks, including vertex classification and link prediction.</p>\n<p>A Supervised GraphWise model consists of two graph convolutional layers followed by several prediction layers.<br />\nThe forward pass through a convolutional layer for a vertex proceeds as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A set of neighbors of the vertex is sampled.</li>\n<li>The previous layer representations of the neighbors are mean-aggregated, and the aggregated features are concatenated with the previous layer representation of the vertex.</li>\n<li>This concatenated vector is multiplied with weights, and a bias vector is added.</li>\n<li>The result is normalized to such that the layer output has unit norm.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The prediction layers are standard neural network layers.</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
        "relations" : [ ],
        "dynamicFormParams" : null
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 6,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%pgql-pgx",
          "",
          "/* Find a filter to split the graph into a train and a test graph */",
          "SELECT v",
          "FROM MATCH (v) ON cora_graph",
          "WHERE v.paper_id % 4 > 0",
          "LIMIT 10"
        ],
